		{
			dependencies: ["750F9DC2755C097F"]
			description: [
				"&o&6Eterna&r is the most basic attribute. &6&oIt determines the max enchanting level&r. Think of it like regular enchanting. The more Eterna you have, the higher level your enchantments will be. Eterna is mostly increased by using stronger bookshelves, but some items such as magical crystals can also increase it when placed nearby."
				"There are several different bookshelves, but for now, let's just use the basic wooden ones."
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/eterna.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
			]
			id: "0626E825BC0B0B77"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "60EB54309487C935"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "2736DCABF4014019"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "itemfilters:tag"
					tag: {
						value: "forge:bookshelves"
					}
				}
				title: "Wooden Bookshelf"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Eterna"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["750F9DC2755C097F"]
			description: [
				"&6&oQuanta is the stat that affects the randomness of your enchantments&r. A range is created based on your level and Quanta. The higher your Quanta, the larger this range is. This can be seen as both a good and bad thing, as you'll have access to stronger enchantments, but the strength will also become less consistent."
				"Quanta can be increased by stronger bookshelves or &o&6by placing skulls near the enchanting table.&r"
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/quanta.png width:156 height:90 align:center}"
			]
			id: "44A41664198FD457"
			rewards: [{
				amount: 100L
				currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
				id: "438885B39C2F94DA"
				ignore_reward_blocking: true
				type: "eternalcurrencies:currency"
			}]
			tasks: [{
